# A shell script checked out with CRLF has "#!/bin/sh\r" as its first line.
# Linux reads that literally, looks for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", and
# reports "no such file or directory" -- naming the script rather than the
# interpreter, so it reads as a missing file. COPY such a script into an image
# and the container will not start. It costs an afternoon every time.
#
# CI never sees this: a Linux checkout is LF already. Only a Windows checkout,
# where core.autocrlf hands out CRLF, produces the broken build.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
